<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Autonomist Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a>–<a href="/years/1916">1916</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Partido Autonomista Nacional</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/autonomist-party-dalmatia">Autonomist Party</a> was the conservative party that dominated Argentine politics from 1874 until 1916, led above all by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julio-argentino-roca">Julio Argentino Roca</a>. It ruled through an alliance of provincial governors and limited, often fraudulent elections, and it presided over the country's export boom and mass immigration until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saenz-pena-law">Sáenz Peña Law</a> opened the way to Radical victory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-autonomist-party.jpg" alt="National Autonomist Party" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HapHaxion · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblema_del_Partido_Autonomista_Nacional.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
